 # Inactive persistent Yard candidate
 
+The historical candidate hub lane deliberately pairs its frozen store (`683272ae…`) with the 40 account-boundary checks from `e2310e966373830768fe19c6a3ed58ddc0a8745e`, already archived and pinned under `history/pre-room-hud/production/tests/hub-account-boundaries.test.mjs` (`6df2ec23…`). The overlay loader retains the original test URL so relative imports still exercise the candidate. The current production lane remains the unchanged 61-check root test (`a4cabd98…`) against the rollback-safe store (`8c7e360e…`), mandatory in `pnpm test`. A candidate boundary assertion verifies both exact pairs and independently probes the native module loader. The historical lane does not claim rollback-retention coverage; production tests provide that coverage. No historical source, archive, assertion, or provenance pin is rewritten to repair this harness mismatch.
+
 The current room-toolbar and entry-art transition follows the cold/Escape proof. `reviewedRoomHudChangeSet` and `history/pre-room-hud/` preserve the exact four approved patches and prior contract, room and test witness bytes. The existing room.json production pin advances from 3,248 bytes / `c1d704329625ee99c9bdaddd2805a2a11531eb3c481b8d0203addfea90e8a2e3` to 3,265 bytes / `c575ff84ed68316091df379c43760424a5513a16893b1904c4d67e7c1020411d`, adding the reviewed 120px small-phone currency width. Five retired public exports, totaling 371,894 bytes, remain byte-identical in source-only archives. Every older contract/history and all 16 closed-control pins remain unchanged. The e231 canonical source/media closure and native fixtures are unchanged. The same unpublished transition also incorporates the approved post-reload saved Sun Cushion render witness: the eight-player spec advances from 18,835 bytes / `0aa5803d455fd0edca6e6d59f7ae32d01db2328f73d19b6e83ebf4a13b8701ac` to 21,209 bytes / `81acce782d8ae756a7206a1c65763090f673a3c4265e7fc36940c0bd498a4d9d`. Both prior test files and patch `25c2296851c4899859c81d59d3174cf26c582dc687b3d2df0a83a395ce2d1dee` are archived. The original cold/Escape record still validates its archived spec; current exact witness bytes are checked by the room transfer. This strengthens the pending browser evidence and does not claim that the new screenshot assertion has already passed. The independently approved rollback outbox fix also advances the useGameHub production pin from 28,619 bytes / `04591b270ab5eca3eea89730211e138342e14964e9e840c2816639c46eac5d33` to 31,889 bytes / `8c7e360eb0d3ced6b6ab3e2a5ebdbc04cea52fc9798b2d1369a36c727569e590`, under exact patch `4f9d12db90a5aead86c1ba9f514716177d753c35ca61bafe60a7755047d4ce49`. The prior store and account-boundary tests are archived. Closed-rollout 409 responses now retain the unresolved nonce, payload and busy lock; replay requires a fresh, ordered, account-current writable HTTP observation. Failed persistence, stale reads, account changes and newer closure observations cannot authorize replay. The original player-wiring transition remains validated against its archived store; only the current production pin advances. Actual browser/real-API CI for the assembled source remains required.
 
 The original cold-duration requirement below remains historical. The later scoped decision in `docs/yard-component-evidence-reuse.md` supersedes it for the reviewed geometry-only repair without claiming that a new duration run completed. Current main/browser/asset CI and separate ACTIVE acceptance remain required; the existing e231 native run continues as additional confidence.
